  message: "Fixed: Merged as PR #1402, dev SHA 3abedae58888 (see the auto-pr entry above). Owner-approved design, 2026-10-03.\nBEHAVIORAL EVIDENCE, re-run on dev 3abedae588:\n1. The filed measurement: load_catalog('python').is_stdlib_module is now True for distutils, distutils.spawn, imp, asyncore, smtpd, binhex (all were False), and also tomllib, cgi, telnetlib. requests stays False.\n2. Label: `hypergumbo survey` on a fixture with `from distutils.spawn import spawn` stamps python:distutils.spawn:0-0:spawn:external_symbol ecosystem=stdlib (was third_party).\n3. Verdict UNCHANGED (the acceptance control): `hypergumbo verify-claims` with \"never spawns a subprocess\" (boundary: subprocess, must_not_exist) returns inconclusive, exit 2: \"makes calls into 1 module(s) that the I/O catalog could not classify (distutils.spawn) ... cannot confirm the boundary is unused.\" Recognition did not examine it.\nTests: test_python_stdlib_versions.py (windows vs the live interpreter; python.yaml covers every window; supported_versions; distutils-still-withholds via compute_boundary_coverage), the e2e ecosystem test, and generator tests (union written; supported_versions mismatch refused). All were red before the change for the right reasons. smart-test 18,960 passed, changed sources at 100% coverage.\nAlso done in the PR: one shared table (hypergumbo_core/python_stdlib_versions.py) now feeds the generator AND the WI-jojuz scope gate; ADR-0016/io_boundary wording updated (the stale \"feeds the F3 filter\" clause dropped); ADR-0041's decaying \"283 of 300\" count removed.\nNOT VERIFIED: the 3.10/3.11/3.13 nightly legs' run of the window test. It checks the table against each real interpreter, and confirmation arrives with the same nightly WI-jojuz is waiting on."  # 13c3
